{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And you shall proclaim release in the land to all its inhabitants; it shall be a jubilee.</b> Rashi, of blessed memory, explained that the occasion is called by the name יובל (jubilee) because they sound the shofar in it, from the language of (Joshua 6:4) במשך בקרן היובל, (ibid.) שופרות היובלים; and so is the view of the commentators." "<b>But</b> the Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote that their explanation is not correct, for in במשך בקרן היובל and שופרות היובלים it is a ram's horn, and its commandment is only on Rosh HaShanah, in order to recall the ram of Isaac; but it is not so on the Day of Atonement, for the Day of Atonement — its commandment is with a yael horn. Therefore he, of blessed memory, explained that it is not called יובל on account of the sounding, but on account of the release (דרור); for if it were called after the sounding, it would have been fitting for Scripture to say 'and you shall pass a shofar of teru'ah in the seventh month, on the tenth of the month — it shall be a יובל'; but it said 'and you shall proclaim release in the land to all its inhabitants — it shall be a יובל,' meaning that they shall all be free men, to dwell wherever they wish. 'It shall be a יובל' — in which every man is brought back (מובל) to his ancestral holding and to his family. And therefore the fruits and produce are also called יבול, from the root meaning 'to bring'; likewise the deep places where waters are are also called (Isaiah 36) פלגים יבלי מים, for there the waters come — end of quotation. And the reason for the commandment of the jubilee by way of the plain sense (peshat) is that all the fields return to their owners, and even the slaves who have been pierced go free at the appointed time of the jubilee; and this is the meaning of יובל, for each and every thing is brought back (יובל) to its ancestral holding and to its family." "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah,</b> יובל היא — from the language of (Jeremiah 17:8) ועל יובל ישלח שרשיו, and it alludes that all the generations are brought back (יובלו) to the first Cause. Therefore the jubilee is called by the name דרור (release), for it is the יובל in which the root of all the generations and all created beings is set, for from there they were emanated in an everlasting covenant, as it says (Genesis 1:1) בראשית ברא אלהים, and there is their return. And understand this: for each of the seven produces seven thousand, and behold they are 49; and when 49 are completed for the world, it will be תהו ובהו (unformed and void) and the totality will return to the יובל just as it was emanated from there — and understand this. And this is the language of Scripture (Leviticus 25:13) בשנת היובל הזאת תשובו איש אל אחזתו, (ibid. 27) בשנת היובל ישוב. And the philosophers of inquiry mentioned in their language: all was from the first Cause, and all returns to the first Cause. And if you merit to understand the secret of the shemittah and the jubilee, what he mentioned regarding the shemittah — שדך כרמך ספיח קצירך ענבי נזיריך — in the second person ('your field,' etc.), will not be hidden from you; for after the year of shemittah passes, which Scripture called 'a sabbath unto HaShem,' which is a sabbath and rest for the life of the worlds, they shall be yours as before. And contemplate the forceful verse in the psalm 'A Song for the Sabbath Day,' which alludes to what will be after the Sabbath, namely what it says (Psalms 92:13) צדיק כתמר יפרח, and it is written (ibid. 72) יפרח בימיו צדיק ורוב שלום עד בלי ירח. And this too is alluded to in the passage of ויכלו, for after he mentioned (Genesis 2) ויברך אלהים את יום השביעי, in order to make known what will be after the seventh day, he sealed the passage with the word לעשות, meaning to make actions and to call the generations from of old. And because of this, regarding the commandment of the shemittah he mentioned שדך כרמך קצירך נזירך — in the manner of 'yours'; but he did not mention thus regarding the jubilee, rather ספיחיה נזיריה, because they are hers and you have nothing in them — and I have already mentioned this in the section of ואלה המשפטים. And from this Scripture says לאשר לו אחזת הארץ — it did not say נחלת הארץ, for the matter of נחלה is what a person inherits from another, but it said אחוזה, which is language indicating the original, essential owners; and this is what is written (Ecclesiastes 5:7) כי גבוה מעל גבוה שומר וגבוהים עליהם, and this is clear."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:28:25.857259472Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}